A complex mechanical pocket watch floating in space, its face opened to reveal intricate gears and cogs that transform into interconnected human silhouettes as they spiral outward from the center. The brass and copper mechanisms have a warm patina, with some gears appearing simplified and streamlined while others branch into elaborate fractal patterns of increasing complexity. Swirling golden nebulae in the background. The watch hands point in multiple directions simultaneously, suggesting the tension between order and chaos. Rendered in the distinctive style of Vincent van Gogh with bold, expressive brushstrokes, rich impasto texture, and characteristic swirling movement in the cosmic background. Deep blues and vibrant yellows dominate the palette, with the mechanical elements rendered in warm ochres and burnt oranges. The brushwork creates a sense of dynamic energy and emotional intensity around the floating timepiece.
